    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0500" n="1234" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1234"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mavroyeni Bey to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial Legation of Turkey</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-29"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of your note of the 27th instant, in which you point out
                    that Mr. Gresham, in my interview with him of the 4th of April last, probably
                    referred to the girls’ college of Scutari.</p>
                <p>As your excellency now informs me that the Imperial firman concerning the
                    above-mentioned concession, spoken of in my note of the 12th instant, has not
                    yet been issued, I propose to write concerning it to the Sublime Porte by the
                    next mail.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mavroyeni Bey.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
